\section{Purpose \& Scope}

The Tissue Regeneration White Sheet establishes the foundational architecture for the
\textbf{Sovereign Regenerative Engine (SRE)}, a multi-scale simulation system designed to model
controlled tissue reconstruction under adversarial biological conditions.

This White Sheet encodes:
\begin{itemize}
  \item the regeneration objective,
  \item the multi-layer substrate architecture,
  \item the invariant framework,
  \item the stability and convergence assumptions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Regeneration Objective}

The SRE aims to simulate:
\begin{itemize}
  \item controlled cellular regrowth,
  \item scaffold-guided tissue formation,
  \item metabolic and immune stability,
  \item vascular integration and nutrient restoration.
\end{itemize}

The engine enforces a triad of regeneration invariants ensuring that reconstructed tissue
remains stable, non-neoplastic, and structurally coherent.

\section{Multi-Layer Architecture}

\subsection{Cellular Layer — Regrowth Logic}

Cellular proliferation is governed by:
\[
\Gamma_{\text{mitosis}}
= \alpha_0 \left(1 - \frac{\rho_0}{\rho_{\max}}\right)
\Theta(\pi - \pi_{\text{crit}}),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $\rho_0$ is local cell density,
  \item $\rho_{\max}$ is saturation density,
  \item $\Theta$ is the Heaviside gating function,
  \item $\pi$ is mechanical pressure.
\end{itemize}

Cellular stability invariant:
\[
R_c:\quad \frac{\partial \rho_c}{\partial t} \le 0
\quad \text{(zero neoplastic drift)}.
\]

\subsection{Structural Layer — Tissue Blueprint}

Mechanical equilibrium:
\[
\nabla \cdot \sigma + f_{\text{ext}} = 0,
\]
with scaffold stability constraint:
\[
R_s:\quad \left\lVert \Delta \text{Scaffold Geometry} \right\rVert
< \epsilon_{\text{tol}}.
\]

\subsection{System Layer — Regenerative Stability}

Capillary ingrowth velocity:
\[
\frac{\partial v_{\text{cap}}}{\partial t}
= k_v\left(\frac{m_{\text{target}} - m}{n_{\text{target}}}\right)
- \gamma_{\text{immune}}.
\]

Metabolic + immune load invariant:
\[
R_m, R_i:\quad
\int (m_{\text{deficit}} + i_{\text{inflammation}})\, dV
\le \delta.
\]

\section{Unified Regeneration Invariant}

The Sovereign Regeneration Invariant is defined as:
\[
\mathcal{R}_{\text{regen}}
= R_c \land R_s \land R_m \land R_i.
\]

When $\mathcal{R}_{\text{regen}}$ holds, the simulation guarantees:
\begin{itemize}
  \item controlled proliferation,
  \item scaffold stability,
  \item metabolic equilibrium,
  \item immune suppression of pathological cascades.
\end{itemize}

\section{Stability \& Convergence}

Define Lyapunov functional $V(\bm{X})$ measuring structural, metabolic, and proliferative
deviation.

Regeneration stability requires:
\[
\frac{dV}{dt} < 0
\quad \forall t \ge t_0.
\]

This ensures monotonic convergence toward a stable reconstructed tissue state.

